    The prevention edit form's Date row (its label cell and its box cell), included by each of
    AddPreventionData.jsp's four layouts (injection, h1n1, PAPMAM, history) so the page has one prevDate
    element, with its label in the same file.

    A stored date of a year, or a year and month, only (partialPrevDate, set by the page) is edited in a
    text box that takes yyyy, yyyy-mm or yyyy-mm-dd; any other date keeps the browser's date input.

    Uses the page's prevDate and partialPrevDate and its carlos taglib, and declares fmt itself (the same
    URI as the page). The fragment's text is written out exactly where it is included: the include sits at
    the label cell's indent, so the box cell's line carries that indent here, and nothing may follow the
    closing tag, not even a newline.
--%><%@ taglib uri="jakarta.tags.fmt" prefix="fmt" %><div class="col-sm-4"><label for="prevDate" class="col-form-label col-form-label-sm fields"><fmt:message key="oscarprevention.addpreventiondata.date"/></label></div>
                                    <div class="col-sm-8"><input type="<%= partialPrevDate ? "text" : "date" %>" class="form-control form-control-sm" name="prevDate"
                                                                                          id="prevDate"
                                                                                          value="<carlos:encode value='<%= prevDate != null && prevDate.length() >= 10 ? prevDate.substring(0, 10) : (prevDate != null ? prevDate : "") %>' context="htmlAttribute"/>"
                                                                                          required<% if (partialPrevDate) { %> pattern="\d{4}(-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])(-(0[1-9]|[12]\d|3[01]))?)?" title="yyyy | yyyy-mm | yyyy-mm-dd"<% } %>></div>